\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Go to dark Gethsemane,
\par Ye that feel the tempter's power
\par Your redeemer's conflict see;
\par Watch with Him one bitter hour;
\par Turn not from His griefs away:
\par Learn of Jesus Christ to pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Follow to the judgment-hall;
\par View the Lord of Life arraigned.
\par O the wormwood and the gall!
\par O the pangs His soul sustained! 
\par Shun not suffering, shame, or loss;
\par Learn to Him to bear the cross.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Calvary's mournful mountain climb;
\par There, adoring at His feet,
\par Mark that miracle of time,
\par God's own sacrifice complete.
\par It is finished! Hear the cry:
\par Learn of Jesus Christ to die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Early to the tomb repair
\par Where they laid His Breathless clay:
\par Angels keep their vigils there; 
\par Who hath taken Him away?
\par Christ is risen! He seeks the skies;
\par Saviour, teach us so to rise.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

